<section style="background:var(--panel);">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <p class="lead">New to TSA? Start here.</p>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">What do we do at meetings? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Members work on their competitive events, collaborate with teammates, plan service projects, and get ready for Regionals, States, and Nationals.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Do I need experience? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>No — TSA has events built for total beginners as well as returning competitors, so there's an entry point for every skill level.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">How do I join? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Attend a chapter meeting, talk to an officer, and complete the membership application on our <a href="resources.html">Resources page</a>.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">What's the difference between Regionals, States, and Nationals? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Every member attends Regionals and States; placing in the top 3 at States qualifies you for Nationals. See the full breakdown on <a href="dates.html">Important Dates</a>.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">What events can I compete in? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>TSA offers dozens of competitions across engineering, coding, media, leadership, and science. Browse them on our <a href="events.html#event-explorer">Events page</a> or take the quiz there to get a recommendation.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
